    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="article-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Notes for picking the right plan mode</p>
        <h1 id="article-title" class="vi-readable-heading">When to use <span class="accent-mark">/ck:plan --deep --tdd</span></h1>
        <p class="dek">Not every task needs the heavy mode. This post breaks down when to reach for <code>--deep</code>, when to add <code>--tdd</code>, and when a shorter route is the better call.</p>
      </div>

      <aside class="hero-card" aria-label="Core idea">
        <p>A big refactor rarely breaks on the first line of code. It usually breaks because the plan didn't see enough scope — and by the time cook runs, the missing tests, migrations, or background jobs have already been skipped.</p>
        <div class="mode-stack">
          <div class="mode"><strong>--deep</strong><span>when scope is wide</span></div>
          <div class="mode"><strong>--tdd</strong><span>when old behavior must survive</span></div>
          <div class="mode"><strong>--deep --tdd</strong><span>when both risks apply</span></div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <button class="mobile-toc-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="toc">Open index</button>

    <div class="layout">
      <nav class="toc" id="toc" aria-label="Contents">
